WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.940
<b>Café Cattleya</b>

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:18.700
Here's your fried shrimp meal.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:25.870
So... I hear from you for 
the first time in a while,

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:30.330
and you want to meet in a place 
like this? What's the deal, Ebitani?

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:33.340
<i>This man is Ebitani.</i>

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:36.340
<i>The man who was fired from 
Teiai after his own mistake,</i>

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:40.350
<i>Team Tonegawa's former 
walking nuclear warhead!</i>

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.350
You're fired!

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:45.800
<i>Ebitani is out!</i>

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>After only one strike.</i>

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:48.940
Your pay is cut!

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:54.320
<i>A shot by a misaligned cannon 
hits Tonegawa hard, sinking him!</i>

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:58.870
<i>Now, these two men have met anew.</i>

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:03.700
<i>What is it Ebitani wants 
to convey to Tonegawa?!</i>

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:11.960
<i>Tonegawa Yukio, the number two 
man of the massive Teiai Group.</i>

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:15.610
<i>He serves the monster 
of the financial sector.</i>

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.970
<i>This shot-caller rose to the position 
of President Hyoudou's right-hand man.</i>

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.670
<i>This is the story of the battles 
he waged as a middle manager,</i>

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:28.070
<i>in the shadows of the glory 
and fame he achieved...</i>

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:36.450
<i>The small, unremarkable story... 
about the struggles of a remarkable man.</i>

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:47.120
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:47.120
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.750
<i>Agenda 08
<b></b></i>Shrimp

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:14.790
<i>Psst...</i>

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:18.800
<i>Psst...</i>

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.890
W-Well, I'm really sorry about...

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:27.910
what happened recently!

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:34.520
I wanted to make up for what 
happened with the president.

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.770
I've felt really guilty about it...

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:38.200
Don't lie to me.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.170
If you really felt that way,

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:43.660
you wouldn't have ordered the deluxe parfait!

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:47.020
At most, you would've 
ordered the coffee jelly.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.410
<i>Psst...</i>

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.860
S-Sorry, sir.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:54.670
<i>This man shows absolutely 
no sign of penitence!</i>

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.960
Would you like some?

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.960
No, I would not! Get that 
spoon out of my face.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.900
And even if you did actually 
want to apologize,

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.690
it's not like that'll undo my cut pay.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:09.970
I'll pay for your ridiculous parfait,

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:11.510
so think about what you've done!

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:14.930
Call me when you're actually 
ready to make it up to me.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:26.230
<i>Several days later...</i>

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.370
Tonegawa-sensei!

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.390
<i>Ebitani reappears!</i>

00:04:35.410 --> 00:04:38.000
Why in the hell have you dragged me out here?

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:42.800
Today, I'll really make it up to you.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:44.980
Not with words, but with action!

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:49.010
Since you suffered a loss because of me,

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:50.980
I've got something valuable...

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:56.770
A deal that'll make up for the 
pay you've lost and then some!

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.180
Psst...

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.550
Right this way. Follow me.

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:06.710
Are you all really enjoying your lives?

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.280
Do you ever worry that you're just

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:13.040
living the same way as everyone else,
when you could be doing more?

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.790
Well, there's a way for 
people like you to succeed!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:20.790
That's right! You have a chance to succeed!

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.050
Even if you're unemployed...

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.430
No! It's only possible 
because you're unemployed!

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.780
By selling this facial 
toner to your neighbors,

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:31.810
you can make a million yen per month!

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:35.980
And if you work hard enough, 
as much as two million!

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.230
<i>Th-This is pretty clearly...</i>

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.230
<i>a seminar for a pyramid scheme!</i>

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:47.840
What do you think, Tonegawa-sensei?

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.870
Is this a revolutionary 
business model or what?

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:56.900
<i>This fool... How dare he bring me, 
a Teiai executive, to a place like this?!</i>

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:02.040
<i>A deep, murky sea, inhabited by a creature 
that calls itself multi-level marketing...</i>

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:08.800
<i>Ebitani, who once haunted 
Tonegawa as a living ghost,</i>

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:13.010
<i>is now a specter attempting to entice 
Tonegawa to sink into the wicked depths,</i>

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.520
<i>where only lost souls dwell!</i>

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:17.380
<i>What an irredeemable imbecile!</i>

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:20.020
<i>And I was a fool for expecting anything else!</i>

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:23.900
I'm leaving.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:26.100
You are?! Why?

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:27.280
It should be obvious!

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:29.270
You're coming, too!

00:06:29.270 --> 00:06:32.410
<i>Even so, Tonegawa can't bring 
himself to abandon Ebitani.</i>

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.290
<i>His compassion is truly remarkable!</i>

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.790
Oh? Is something wrong, you two?

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:42.480
Every single thing about this 
is wrong. We're leaving.

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.140
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:47.090
What? Leaving? Why?

00:06:47.090 --> 00:06:52.220
Don't you realize that leaving now will 
mean letting this opportunity slip away?

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:53.970
Like letting a huge fish off the line!

00:06:53.970 --> 00:07:00.540
He's right, Tonegawa-sensei! You won't 
find a better way to make easy money.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.770
You fool! There's no such 
thing as easy money!

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:06.870
<i>Psst...</i>

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:09.750
It's a huge mistake to think

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:14.410
you can make real money without
putting any real effort in!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.040
Making a million yen a month is the 
kind of thing that talented people

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.290
build up to gradually, 
climbing to it step by step,

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.790
and only after that effort do they reach it.

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:30.100
What's so funny?

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.700
Did you all hear him?!

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.540
This guy is talking about working 
your way up, in this day and age!

00:07:36.540 --> 00:07:38.810
What a dinosaur!

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.060
A confused old man!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:43.060
He's absolutely archaic!

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:47.370
<i>Tonegawa is confronted with 
a wall of feverish fervor!</i>

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:50.440
<i>It's a wipe-out by the 
pyramid scheme's big wave!</i>

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.890
<i>It's too late for any of them...</i>

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:58.080
<i>They're worn out past the point of all help.</i>

00:07:58.550 --> 00:08:01.390
<i>Faced with the scorn of 
the unreasonable crowd,</i>

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:05.080
<i>Tonegawa finds himself 
isolated on enemy turf!</i>

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:10.380
Look, I don't care how you 
people earn your money,

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:15.970
or what trouble it gets any 
of you into, for that matter.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:20.970
But this idiot here 
still owes me an apology.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:25.020
Not the kind he can sub-let to someone else. 
It's something he has to do personally!

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:29.380
<i>It's a flash of insight. 
Tonegawa's words jar something loose.</i>

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:35.740
<i>Ebitani hears the voice from within, 
like that of a divine will. An oracle!</i>

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.740
<b>Divine Message</b>

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:35.740
<b>Oracle</b>

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:48.920
Laugh all you want.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.350
Let's go, Ebitani.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.420
T-Tonegawa-sensei...

00:08:58.090 --> 00:09:01.770
It's not a pyramid scheme... 
It's network business!

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:05.850
<i>A shock strikes Tonegawa!</i>

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:09.440
<i>H-He's in deep!</i>

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.430
<i>Already too far gone to save!</i>

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:16.280
<i>Tragedy! Ebitani has already 
become a lost soul!</i>

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.530
<i>He seriously thinks I'm being a hard-headed,</i>

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:23.790
<i>old man with outdated thinking!</i>

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:30.490
<i>Tonegawa returns home, bitter over his 
inability to show Ebitani the light!</i>

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:40.800
Excuse me, sir.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.060
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:09:44.130 --> 00:09:45.930
It's a letter from Ebitani.

00:09:45.930 --> 00:09:48.440
From Ebitani?!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:54.320
<i>Dear Tonegawa-sensei,</i>

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.740
<i>Thank you for your advice the other day.</i>

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.540
<i>How have you been since then?</i>

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.160
<i>After we talked,</i>

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:04.470
<i>I ultimately ended up dropping out 
of the business deal we discussed.</i>

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:09.360
<i>I remembered the things you told me,</i>

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.920
<i>and even if it was a bit late, 
I came to my senses.</i>

00:10:13.160 --> 00:10:16.230
<i>I guess even that fool had 
to catch on eventually.</i>

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.900
<i>The entire group was later charged</i>

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:21.430
<i>with breaking the 
Commercial Transactions Law,</i>

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.680
<i>and they were all arrested.</i>

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:25.670
See? I knew it.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:31.770
<i>You were right after all. It really 
was a malicious pyramid scheme.</i>

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.400
<i>If you don't mind, I'd still like 
to make all this up to you one day.</i>

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.320
<i>From Ebitani, in the Kosuge Detention Center.</i>

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:44.080
Idiot!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.620
You figured it out too late!

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.290
<i>Ebitani: busted.</i>

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:55.960
Man, this sucks.

00:10:55.960 --> 00:10:58.970
<b>Café Cattleya</b>

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.730
Here's your fried shrimp meal.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:15.340
Well, it's a good thing

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:18.420
that you were released after 
being found innocent, Ebitani.

00:11:18.420 --> 00:11:19.580
Yes, sir!

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.650
<i>Ebitani returns!</i>

00:11:21.650 --> 00:11:25.120
I'm really sorry for the trouble.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:29.120
You'd better be. 
So, what do you want today?

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:32.600
Because if this is anything like last time...

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:33.630
Yes, I know.

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:36.350
I'll get straight to the point.

00:11:36.350 --> 00:11:38.760
Tonegawa-sensei, I am here...

00:11:39.240 --> 00:11:42.510
to convince you to quit Teiai!

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:45.060
<i>Psst...</i>

00:11:46.840 --> 00:11:47.960
Something wrong?

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.280
No... go on.

00:11:50.280 --> 00:11:51.140
Right!

00:11:51.590 --> 00:11:55.270
I met this guy named Inoue 
while I was locked up...

00:11:55.650 --> 00:11:57.410
Listen here, Ebitani-han.

00:11:57.410 --> 00:12:02.530
Crooked financing companies, 
like Teiai, they're trending down!

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:05.830
You're lucky you got out when you did!

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:08.950
We're living in an era 
where one bright idea can

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.410
score you a home run that puts 
you ahead of everybody else!

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.610
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:15.750
A home run?

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:19.420
Yes, sir! And what I came up 
with after hearing that...

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:21.670
was this!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.600
What... is it?

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:24.680
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.370
A whole shrimp fried at a high temperature

00:12:28.370 --> 00:12:30.180
and wrapped up in dough!

00:12:31.130 --> 00:12:32.060
I've named it...

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:35.060
The Ebi Roll!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:38.570
<i>The Ebi Roll is born!</i>

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:38.570
<b>Ebi Roll</b>

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:40.320
<i>Ebi Roll!</i>

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:40.320
<b>Ebi Roll</b>

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.450
<i>Ebi Roll!</i>

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.450
<b>Ebi Roll</b>

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.400
Ebi... Roll?

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:49.510
I asked 3,000 youngsters in Harajuku:

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:53.620
Do you like shrimp? Yes or no?

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:02.490
And to my shock... over 90% 
said that they do like it!

00:12:56.000 --> 00:13:03.130
<b>Do you like shrimp?</b>

00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.630
I'm predicting the rise 
of a major shrimp boom.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:09.400
W-Wait a second. 
Are you telling me you're...

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.760
<i>Psst...</i>

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:14.140
Are you trying to rope me into this?

00:13:15.780 --> 00:13:16.900
Bingo!

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:21.650
With my idea and your funding, 
we can make this happen.

00:13:22.150 --> 00:13:23.670
The Ebi Roll!

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:25.550
<b>Ebi Roll:
Shrimp Whirlwind</b>

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:31.240
<i>A shining sun! The roar of a big wave!</i>

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:34.310
<i>The time has come to kick 
up a shrimp whirlwind!</i>

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:38.210
<i>Ebi Roll! Ebi Roll!</i>

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:41.670
<i>Ebi Goal!</i>

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:43.170
<i>Psst...</i>

00:13:43.690 --> 00:13:47.570
<i>Tonegawa is speechless at this 
completely unanticipated proposal!</i>

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:51.320
What do you think, sir?

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:52.290
Fool!

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:54.220
What do I think?! What else could I think?!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:57.230
I mean, almost everyone likes shrimp!

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:00.320
Are you a shrimp man, too, Tonegawa-sensei?

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.340
Idiot! I'm saying you're asking 
people the wrong question!

00:14:03.340 --> 00:14:05.150
Who would eat this thing?!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.640
Come on, sir, you have to try it 
before you make up your mind.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.190
It's freshly made!

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:14.310
<i>It is this very enthusiasm 
that makes him Ebitani.</i>

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.250
<i>And so, the next day...</i>

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:25.510
Ebi Roll Taste Test

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:22.740
<i>An Ebi Roll taste test is held 
at Teiai's special kitchen.</i>

00:14:23.270 --> 00:14:25.510
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.630
It's been a while, gentlemen. 
It's me, Ebitani.

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:33.730
I think Tonegawa-sensei 
filled you all in already,

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:36.890
but today we're going to be 
trying out my all-new idea

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.840
for a dish made using shrimp.

00:14:38.840 --> 00:14:44.380
I've borrowed this space to have 
you all try out my Ebi Roll.

00:14:45.270 --> 00:14:48.150
<i>I see he's still passionate, if nothing else.</i>

00:14:48.670 --> 00:14:51.790
Does he not feel the least bit awkward?

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.960
Coming back to Teiai after being fired...

00:14:54.410 --> 00:14:57.250
Well... that's about what 
I'd expect from Ebitani.

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:00.080
Now then, everyone, I have here

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:05.100
the fifteen reasons I decided 
to create the Ebi Roll.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:07.930
I'd like to go over those now.

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:10.250
Take a look at the 
documentation I've passed out.

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.760
Ebitani Presents:
15 Reasons Why I Made the Ebi Roll

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.570
First is...

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.960
Enough prelude. Get cooking.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:16.710
Everyone's hungry.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:19.270
I see! Well, in that case...

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:25.400
And this is the eye of this 
particular culinary storm...

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.260
The most high-grade of shrimp: 
the Japanese lobster!

00:15:29.010 --> 00:15:31.770
<i>A single one costs over 8,000 yen!</i>

00:15:31.770 --> 00:15:34.450
<i>It's fine dining with the Japanese lobster!</i>

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:38.450
Now, time to start cooking!

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:45.170
Then...

00:15:45.510 --> 00:15:52.510
We drop our high-grade Japanese lobster 
into oil that's heated to 180 degrees.

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:53.800
That's hot!

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:58.180
Once it's nice and fried...

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.850
Drop it onto the fresh red lettuce!

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.980
Add a little tartar sauce...

00:16:05.460 --> 00:16:10.730
Then wrap it up in a custom-made
corn and flour based wrap!

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.990
And it's ready! This is my Ebi Roll!

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:19.010
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:22.250
Go ahead.

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.500
Come on, everyone, come and get yours!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.500
Don't be shy!

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.460
You, too, Kikuchi-san!

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:35.550
Go ahead and chow down, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:16:35.550 --> 00:16:36.710
Take a big bite!

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:38.760
R-Right...

00:16:47.050 --> 00:16:49.650
What do you think of my Ebi Roll?

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.450
How do I put this?

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:58.450
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:00.120
It stings.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:04.330
<i>A bite of a whole lobster? Dangerous!</i>

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:07.130
The shell is stabbing the 
inside of my mouth. It hurts.

00:17:07.650 --> 00:17:11.140
This is gonna hurt our jaws, Tonegawa-san!

00:17:11.140 --> 00:17:13.380
Maybe you should prepare it another way...

00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.110
Yeah... Sashimi style, maybe.

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:17.010
Or in a pasta.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:20.790
Aw, come on! That can't be 
true, can it, Kawasaki-san?

00:17:22.310 --> 00:17:23.450
Yamazaki-san?!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:33.650
Doushita-san?

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:38.550
I'm sorry!

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:42.050
<i>Psst... Psst...</i>

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:46.210
Seems that confirms it.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.460
Soy-preserved grasshoppers, frog sausage...

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:52.860
Doushita has the kind of appetite that 
lets him finish practically anything,

00:17:52.860 --> 00:17:56.100
but even he has rejected the Ebi Roll.

00:17:58.450 --> 00:18:01.640
Naturally, I won't be 
investing in it, either.

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:07.890
<i>Critical damage! Ebitani's life is at zero.</i>

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:14.660
I'm sure your firing and everything else 
has you in a rush to regain your footing,

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:18.330
but the only ones who can turn things 
around with a single home run are

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:20.530
those who've worked hard 
to empower themselves!

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:22.030
Stop looking for short-term gains.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:25.010
There is no victory without perseverance.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:31.720
I bought it, though...

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.670
I thought this was a sure-fire 
win, so I already...

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:39.930
bought 200 kilograms of 
frozen Japanese lobster!

00:18:42.360 --> 00:18:43.930
<i>Psst...</i>

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:47.340
<i>Ebitani acts characteristically reckless!</i>

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:49.920
Idiot! Why would you get that much?!

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.690
Because it was cheaper to buy in bulk

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:55.190
as opposed to per-unit!

00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:59.080
What now?

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:11.320
Y'know, I've been in the 
mood for shrimp lately.

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:14.090
Send me 30,000 yen worth.

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:19.340
Thank you so much, Tonegawa-sensei!

00:19:19.340 --> 00:19:24.220
Y'know, miso soup made with Japanese 
lobster is supposed to be tasty.

00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:28.650
I'll take some, too. 10,000 yen worth.

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:31.030
20,000 for Gonda.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:32.440
10,000 for Doushita.

00:19:32.440 --> 00:19:34.230
10,000 for Ogino.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:35.730
10,000 for Kawasaki.

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:36.820
And 10,000 for Hagio.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.010
I'll take 10,000 yen worth, too.

00:19:39.010 --> 00:19:40.810
10,000 yen for me, too.

00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:42.320
5,000 yen for Nakata...

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:44.820
You guys...

00:19:45.350 --> 00:19:47.800
Thank you so much!

00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:53.810
<i>The ring of compassion links 
Team Tonegawa together!</i>

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:58.530
Thank you for your business!

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:06.350
Excuse me.

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:08.600
Tonegawa-sensei...

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.480
It's a letter from Ebitani.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:12.980
What?

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:18.050
<i>Dear Tonegawa-sensei,</i>

00:20:18.690 --> 00:20:21.050
<i>Thank you for what you did the other day.</i>

00:20:21.990 --> 00:20:25.700
<i>The events of that day have helped me 
realize that when I take extreme action,</i>

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:29.590
<i>the results tend to be poor.</i>

00:20:30.970 --> 00:20:33.460
<i>Took you long enough, fool.</i>

00:20:33.800 --> 00:20:39.030
<i>And as ridiculous as it might seem, 
seeing you all buy those frozen lobsters</i>

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.060
<i>helped me realize something.</i>

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:44.500
<i>The natural appeal of shrimp...</i>

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.130
<i>Its true potential!</i>

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:51.980
<i>I, Ebitani, have decided to risk 
it all and buy one ton of lobster!</i>

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:56.880
Idiot! Give me my 30,000 back!

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.610
<i>Everything's turning up 
lobster for Tonegawa!</i>

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:03.530
<i>But hang in there, Tonegawa. 
Don't give up, Tonegawa.</i>

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:08.620
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer</i>

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:12.090
<i>and his own employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:12.530 --> 00:21:15.370
<i>And sometimes, one of his ex-employees.</i>

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:19.920
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.080
Ugh!

00:22:55.170 --> 00:22:57.110
<i>Next time: "Cutlets"!</i>

00:22:55.930 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Cutlets</b>
